{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489016-search-inspiration-for-psionic-power-rotes","id":1489016,"title":"Search inspiration for Psionic power/rotes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-03T14:31:15-07:00","id":1489016,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Search inspiration for Psionic power/rotes","content":"Dear psionics. I ran into a lack of ideas. I have a psionic, but I want to give him psi powers or rotes that fit the paradigm. I have not yet decided whether it will be a normal psionic or an awakened one.<br /> The task looks simple, but the problem is that I'm trying to create some non-standard powers.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to come up with a couple of concepts:<br /> - Use of force (gravity, kinetic force, possibly with other parts of physics; but without &quot;elemental&quot; magic - fire/lightning, etc.) This is not a psionicist who creates fire and lightning, we are not reality deviants.<br /> - Attack psionics or perhaps tormenting psionics? The concept of calling suffering, pain and other things. The problem here is that I can't think of anything more than instilling pain into the target's brain with Mind.<br /> - However, I will not refuse other ideas (healing psionics?, well, we saw this) and advice.<br /> <br /> Mages have the ability to combine spheres and create interesting effects. And I could take ideas from other lines, books, movies or whatever, but sometimes I need a lot of spheres to mimic those powers, which limits me a lot. So I thought it might be easier to start with a regular psionic with 2 &quot;psi-paths&quot;. But such psionics do not have the &quot;paths&quot; I need.<br /> That's why I hope that maybe someone here created homemade psi-powers or interesting rotes. As a technocrat, he has Mind/Force/Life, but maybe I'll replace one of them with Data.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T16:07:11-07:00","id":1489024,"title":"","content":"So, in my games, I actually consider that most of the awakened ones that never meet another Mage for a long enough period of time, most of the time develops &quot;psionic powers&quot;; there is, this is what those people believe. With a total lack of any explanations as to all the crushing amount of weirdness and bizarre, those poor sods try to make some sense to the madness around them.<br /> <br /> And Mages are too rare, too rare to be able to be everywhere that a new awakened shows up.<br /> <br /> So, those without mentors end up believing they developed psionics. At least for the most part, and at least in the modern age. Sure, some still think they've been possessed or cursed by demons or blessed by angels, but a good amount nowadays go for &quot;I have psionic powers&quot; and become self made &quot;mages&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for rotes, psionics could in theory do ALL the effects from ALL spheres. &quot;Psionic teleport&quot; with correspondence, psionic transmutation with matter and even psionic spirit.<br /> <br /> What can or cant be done in a Technocrat paradigm will have to be determined by you.<br /> <br /> That been said, some effects are more adequate than others. Spirit and Mind powers in particularly are excellent for the most part, especially Mind. Telepathy (Mind 3) and Telesend (also Mind 3, the ability to send your own thoughts into other minds). In other uses of Telesend, it's the creation of mental illusions - which are a form of sending thoughts into other minds, but &quot;sensorial thoughts&quot; instead of &quot;memory thoughts&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, on the other end of the telepathic powers, you have those psionics who are <i>Empaths</i>. Empaths deal with emotions, emotional manipulation rather than the more crude mental domination. This is all done with Mind 2. An Empathy look into his victim, press his finger to his head and makes the victim get an irresistible sexual drive, or explode into a mad bloodlust rage attack. Or anything more subtle than that in the inbetween. The empath can cause excruciating pain, can put a person to sleep with a relaxing effect, can cause fear, rage, sadness, joy, induce frenetic maniac episodes of boundless energy as if the victim has snort cocaine etc. So, while Empaths do not exert direct control on others, it is a massive power still nonetheless (if you play VtM, just think that everything that Presence does, an Empath can do with Mind 2). Empaths can also &quot;read&quot; a person's general mood and superficial thoughts.<br /> <br /> You said that &quot;fire is from reality deviants&quot;, but I totally disagree. Have you ever seen the first Hellboy movie? Not a great movie but alas... Anyway, Hellboy's &quot;girlfriend&quot; was a psionic girl that could control fire... Well, she wasnt very good at the &quot;control&quot; part, which also means she's dangerous, but...<br /> <br /> Anyway, in here we have two powers that are classic psionic powers, and those are: Pyrokinesis and Cryokinesis. Respectivelly, the power to control Fire and the power to control Ice, to heat up and to cool down.<br /> <br /> Moving stuff around is Telekinesis, which is more know than the two powers above.<br /> <br /> Likewise, there's also a psionic power that deals with electromagnetics, but I dont remember the name. If you dont want that thou, it aint a problem at all - the guy is still a tech-boy, right? Well, for electromagnetics he may still need to use physics and engineering in order to build machines, for the rest he simply uses the &quot;power of his brain&quot;.<br /> <br /> Gravity is just &quot;high level telekinesis&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;Psionic Healing&quot; is another classic. Some psionics have the ability to &quot;strenghten their bodies&quot; using their psionic powers - that's Life 3. Life 1 can serve for psionic divination powers - so for example, guiving a medical diagnosis, Psionic Life 1, or Sense Life, also Psionic Life 1.<br /> <br /> If you think that shapeshifiting is out of place, your tech can still go for the good old mad lab for those, that's your call, althought I wouldnt say that it is something completely off.<br /> <br /> Now, lets add some variation. Instead of just simply placing his hands in his head and shitting his pants, there are some alternatives for rotes.<br /> <br /> Remember Professor Xavier and the &quot;Brain Computer&quot;?<br /> <br /> Well, the Computer is what we call a <b>Psicothronics</b>. Psicothronics usually are electronic devices (machines, not to be confused with techie wonders) that <i>&quot;amplify&quot;</i> psionic powers.<br /> <br /> Now, those are just simply custom taylored focuses; the whole &quot;amplify psionic powers&quot; is just &quot;techno-babble&quot;, like everything else about magik (enhancing crystals? Special herbs? All mystic babble).<br /> <br /> Be that as it may, your psionic user <i>may</i> be a Telepath... But he's not very good at it.<br /> <br /> But worry not, because his &quot;Telepathic Helmet&quot; (a ridiculous metal hat filled with silly circuits and buttoms) helps him &quot;focus his powers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Those could even be standard equipment for Enlighten agents - in a less silly version, the trademark signature of the NWO, the dark glasses, could be powerful &quot;psicothronic devices&quot;, serving as the focus of several psionic powers (and possibly enhanced with several other electronic functions, both magik and mundane, like a HUD screen with internet connection and facial recognition program, similar to the screen of Iron Man, night vision etc).<br /> <br /> Besides that, other good focuses are always some good old DRUGS. &quot;Hyper Glandule Stimulation&quot; drug to induce your Empathic powers to kick in, etc.<br /> <br /> And lastly, self hypnosis techniques. That's basically a special form of meditation. Those can range from looking to a computer screen with randomly generated colors, to closing your eyes and saying &quot;ohm... ohm... ohm&quot; in order to get glimpses of the future or &quot;feeling thoughts&quot; around you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T16:22:46-07:00","id":1489026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489016-search-inspiration-for-psionic-power-rotes#post1489016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mages have the ability to combine spheres and create interesting effects. And I could take ideas from other lines, books, movies or whatever, but sometimes I need a lot of spheres to mimic those powers, which limits me a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Spheres can actually create A TON of &quot;psionic powers&quot;. In fiction, while some psiquics have a ton of powers, many times they only have one or two. You can represent this in 3 ways:<br /> <br /> Your tech is a Telepath, and ONLY a Telepath. That's fine; this means that the only effect that he can use which will have Psionics as a focus will be &quot;Mind 3: Telepathy&quot;. Fine.<br /> <br /> Your psiquic may have LATENT powers - there is, he has the POTENTIAL to &quot;have&quot; psionics (there is, he believes or is led to believe in that potential), but is unable to naturally access those; in that case, he needs some sort of Psycotronics (silly &quot;telepathic hats&quot;, drugs or special meditation techniques). Once again, this may be limited to a few effects or not; he may be a Cryomancer, Telekinetic and Telepath, but not an Empath or Pyromancer.<br /> <br /> Since in the universe of Mage &quot;psionic powers&quot; are just a form of self illusion - but then again, so too is the Hermetic &quot;magic&quot; or the Technocratic &quot;Science&quot; - the extension of the &quot;latent psionic powers&quot; a techie have is entirely what the techie believes himself to be capable of doing. If you go to the Progenitor doctor, and after testing you he says &quot;Johnny boy, you are a natural Cryomancer and Empathy&quot;, you'll interiorize that, and from that moment onwards you'll use your &quot;psionic abilities&quot; to create ice and manipulate emotions AND NOTHING ELSE, because that's what you believe that it is what you can do. And, for manipulating electromagnetic energy, you'll need your &quot;energon-3000&quot; machine to so, while for creating ice you just close your eyes and contract your muscles.<br /> <br /> And, it's even possible that, someday later, you end up discovering that you're also a telepath, and that you probably had this additional &quot;latent power&quot; which the good ol' doctor failed to identify in the first inspection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T04:35:32-07:00","id":1489090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489016-search-inspiration-for-psionic-power-rotes?p=1489026#post1489026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Spheres can actually create A TON of &quot;psionic powers&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know a lot can be done. But I'm interested in the variety of practices or applications of certain types of psi-powers or forces.<br /> <br /> Let's take fire as an example. Some mystical creature can: form a fireball and throw it at a wall, can make a knife hot, can put out a fire, can form a wall of fire or an elemental, turn other energy (lightning) or matter (blood) into fire, possibly mystical transformation into fire or coating self with fire armor.<br /> Technomages can emit heat waves and dry up the ground. And we have not touched on balefire yet - a cursed flame that can burn souls, melt the body and even mutate it into a pile of cancerous meat.<br /> <br /> But what about gravity, kinetic force, or suggestion of pain/discomfort? Especially if we are a psionic and not a mystic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 08-04-2022, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T05:03:09-07:00","id":1489094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489016-search-inspiration-for-psionic-power-rotes?p=1489090#post1489090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know a lot can be done. But I'm interested in the variety of practices or applications of certain types of psi-powers or forces.<br /> <br /> Let's take fire as an example. Some mystical creature can: form a fireball and throw it at a wall, can make a knife hot, can put out a fire, can form a wall of fire or an elemental, turn other energy (lightning) or matter (blood) into fire, possibly mystical transformation into fire or coating self with fire armor.<br /> Technomages can emit heat waves and dry up the ground. And we have not touched on balefire yet - a cursed flame that can burn souls, melt the body and even mutate it into a pile of cancerous meat.<br /> <br /> But what about gravity, kinetic force, or suggestion of pain/discomfort? Especially if we are a psionic and not a mystic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Errr... I talked about all of that - and more. Just read the rest that I wrote, instead of just the 2 first lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T05:38:01-07:00","id":1489098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489016-search-inspiration-for-psionic-power-rotes?p=1489094#post1489094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Errr...</div> </div> </div> </div>I read. There are variations of different types of psionics and ways to enhance it. This is a good text with good examples of possible powers. But that (my last) question is about usage or flexibility.<br /> Mystics can do many thing with <b>fire </b>- turn it into swords and animals. But, I look at this gravity and my psionic... and I think - gravity is a useful thing on a global scale, but there is little that can be done with it. I came up with options with the creation of grav-sphere or field, grav-wave or remote explosion due to a pressure / gravity difference. But, either this is the limit for gravity on such a scale, or I have a lack of ideas.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the psionics (or techno paradigm) is somewhat limited in physical manipulation. I'll try to compensate for this with cyber-implants or a useful device.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T05:56:30-07:00","id":1489100,"title":"","content":"One of the cool things about Mage it's that you, the player, gets to think about, and to some extent <i>decide</i>, how the world works. A mage doesn't simply &quot;have powers&quot;, a mage defined on individual powers would need an endless character sheet, what they have instead it's a whole cosmology (or a whole <i>narration</i>, in the roleplaying sense) that they can use together with the rules as a &quot;well&quot; to exctract and excert powers<br /> <br /> So: Think about how your character believes the universe works <i>trough </i>psionics, rather than just how psionics works inside the universe.<br /> <br /> What IS &quot;a cursed flame that can burn souls&quot;?, What are &quot;curses&quot;?, What are &quot;souls&quot;?, do these things even exist?. Is it superstitious thing to define something they don't understand, but that could be <i>studied</i> and then <i>defined </i>as a phisical element that then could be the subject of your &quot;psionic waves&quot; or whatever?<br /> <br /> Psionics in fiction (and even RL) it's so random, that you can easily adapt pretty much anything.<br /> <br /> Like, one philosophical concept that can be adapted for psionics that I really like it's that of the<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noosphere\" target=\"_blank\"> N</a><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noosphere\" target=\"_blank\">oosphere</a>(that's a real life concept, but also used in D&amp;D and Numenera for Psionics). Trough a psionical manipulation of it it you could access boundless information about the world, and even alter it in a very flexible way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-04-2022, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T06:21:09-07:00","id":1489101,"title":"","content":"I know... just not enough imagination to work with kinetics/gravity.<br /> <br /> Local Noosphere with psionic Force/Life manipulation... i think we re-created Stalker game. Thats definitely unusual source for inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 08-04-2022, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T07:42:13-07:00","id":1489110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489016-search-inspiration-for-psionic-power-rotes?p=1489098#post1489098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I read. There are variations of different types of psionics and ways to enhance it. This is a good text with good examples of possible powers. But that (my last) question is about usage or flexibility.<br /> Mystics can do many thing with <b>fire </b>- turn it into swords and animals. But, I look at this gravity and my psionic... and I think - gravity is a useful thing on a global scale, but there is little that can be done with it. I came up with options with the creation of grav-sphere or field, grav-wave or remote explosion due to a pressure / gravity difference. But, either this is the limit for gravity on such a scale, or I have a lack of ideas.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the psionics (or techno paradigm) is somewhat limited in physical manipulation. I'll try to compensate for this with cyber-implants or a useful device.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Changing the direction of gravity for the psychic so he can walk up walls. As an effect it is nearly identical to putting a constant force on himself so that should be Forces 2 or 3.<br /> <br /> Indeed, gravity manipulation can be the explanation for a lot of standard telekinetic effects. Usually there wouldn't even be a change to the spheres.<br /> <br /> A simple manipulation of gravity in the vicinity of someone's legs would be a good justification for increasing difficulty levels or tripping them up. Strictly speaking that's not targeted at their legs directly so it should just be Forces 2.<br /> <br /> You can also rapidly alter the pull of gravity on a subject's digestive tract which will very likely cause abdominal distress and an intense need to go to the bathroom. That's a Forces 2/Life 2 or just Life 2 depending on how you are adjudicating (that's a topic for another thread). <br /> <br /> If your gravity manipulation includes mass manipulation, you can get into a bunch of the Matter effects as well. Dropping the mass of an object just long enough to throw it or fire it normally would be a good way to use Matter to increase successes on a ranged attack. You could accelerate it magically too, but I'm not sure there's much benefit to using a Matter/Forces combo to do something you could already do (in paradigm) with Forces alone.<br /> <br /> Depending on worldview, you could even justify using your gravity manipulation to make insubstantial things like spirits dense and coherent enough to interact with. That's is, you can use it as justification for some Spirit/Dimensional Science effects.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T08:56:50-07:00","id":1489114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489016-search-inspiration-for-psionic-power-rotes?p=1489098#post1489098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I read. There are variations of different types of psionics and ways to enhance it. This is a good text with good examples of possible powers. But that (my last) question is about usage or flexibility.<br /> Mystics can do many thing with <b>fire </b>- turn it into swords and animals. But, I look at this gravity and my psionic... and I think - gravity is a useful thing on a global scale, but there is little that can be done with it. I came up with options with the creation of grav-sphere or field, grav-wave or remote explosion due to a pressure / gravity difference. But, either this is the limit for gravity on such a scale, or I have a lack of ideas.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the psionics (or techno paradigm) is somewhat limited in physical manipulation. I'll try to compensate for this with cyber-implants or a useful device.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may make a suggestion, Gurps Psionics, Gurps Psionic Powers and Gurps Psi Tech would do wonders for you.<br /> <br /> And dont worry, you dont actually need to learn how to play Gurps in order to use those; in fact, many people use many Gurps supplements as a helping source for many different games, without even knowing how Gurps works, without having ever looked at Gurps Basic Set. I for instance use Gurps Thaumatology, Gurps Fantasy and Gurps Horror A LOT for my Mage games, because they are exceptional in the amount of description that they give. Gurps takes on Psionics is absolutely amazing, if you want a better picture of the limits and capabilities of those, I'd recommend taking a look at those books, and dont worry too much about the mechanics, just look at the descriptions. They also describe campaign uses, what's the impact those have in a world, society, theories behind those, and if I recall, they even describe the origin of the real life ideas about psionic abilities. Give it a try, I promisse you wont regreat it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T09:01:21-07:00","id":1489115,"title":"","content":"There's also Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T09:07:07-07:00","id":1489117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489016-search-inspiration-for-psionic-power-rotes?p=1489114#post1489114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gurps...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, and this was kept a secret from people? Thanks<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489016-search-inspiration-for-psionic-power-rotes?p=1489115#post1489115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 08-04-2022, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T09:09:32-07:00","id":1489118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurps Psis, pag 4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">PSIONIC POWER<br /> A psi\u2019s power doesn\u2019t have to mesh with his other capa-<br /> bilities. After all, the world is full of people with diverse<br /> and unrelated talents! But some synergy between skills and<br /> psionic abilities can help improve in-game effectiveness. To<br /> make this easier, the templates in Chapter 2 offer advice<br /> regarding appropriate powers. When using a different tem-<br /> plate \u2013 or creating a psi from scratch \u2013 it\u2019s helpful to consider<br /> the role the psychic will play, based on his skills and advan-<br /> tages, and choose a power that complements this. For exam-<br /> ple, a thoughtful, knowledgeable scholar might have ESP,<br /> while an active, impulsive scout should consider Teleportation.<br /> After choosing the power (or powers \u2013 see below), all that<br /> remains is to pick abilities that work well together. If using the<br /> premade psionics packages in Chapter 3, this has already been<br /> accounted for. Otherwise, picturing the psi in action may be<br /> useful when determining whether one ability complements the<br /> other. Of course, the most important rule is to select abilities<br /> that will be fun to play!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just a small note from Gurps Psis - one of the supplements exclusively for this, just to give a small sample. Im gonna be honest, I never liked psionic powers very much, neither in fiction, nor RPG, nor in Gurps or even Mage the Ascension, to me it always sounded like cheap magic for Sci Fi. I prefer &quot;ultratech&quot; or fantasy magic. So, I have those supplements, but never really used them all too much... Let me check my books a little to see if there's something else that is cool to add and I'll get back to you, or if it peaked your interest, go ahead and get those for yourself, since it may help enrich your gameplay","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T09:39:30-07:00","id":1489125,"title":"","content":"And I just found a little thing that is a great example of how those can help, just a small detail but that can help give you some color to your campaign<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurps Psis pag 13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Power Based Disadvantages</b><br /> <br /> While a psychic will generally have several \u201cnormal\u201d<br /> disadvantages \u2013 mental hang-ups, social problems, and physical ailments that anyone might have \u2013 it\u2019s just as appropriate for him to take disadvantages that represent \u201cpside effects\u201d of his power(s) or a particular mindset associated with its abilities. In addition to the traits below, any psi might have Code of Honor (Psychic\u2019s) (p. 6), unless his abilities are strictly self-directed.<br /> Below, exotic and supernatural disadvantage are<br /> marked with an asterisk (*). These are appropriate only for those who possess the associated power; e.g., a psychic vampire can take Lifebane, while an<br /> esper cannot. The GM (<i>Game Master/Storyteller</i>) is welcome to rule otherwise, of course. Other disadvantages are available to anyone \u2013 they just happen to be particularly appropriate for certain types of psi.<br /> <u>Anti-Psi:</u> Intolerance (Psis); Mundane Background (when combined with nothing but passive abilities). <i>(My own personal note: &quot;Anti-Psi&quot; could be attained using Prime as &quot;countermagik&quot;. Your psionic ability is geared toward nulifying other psionic abilities)</i><br /> <u>Astral Projection:</u> Compulsive Snooping<br /> (p. 6); Enemies (Astral entities).<br /> <u>Ergokinesis:</u> Compulsive Snooping (p. 6) (for cyberpsis); Electrical*; Epilepsy.<br /> <u>ESP:</u> Chronic Pain (p. 6); Compulsive Snooping; Confused; Curious; Epilepsy; Flashbacks; Nightmares; Phantom Voices.<br /> <u>Probability Alteration:</u> Klutz or Total Klutz (<i>Personal Note: this is a Gurps Disadvantage for disastrous people, like Goofy and others</i>), Phobia<br /> (Number 13); Unluckiness; Weirdness Magnet*.<br /> <u>Psychic Healing:</u> Charitable; Chummy or Gregarious (p. 6); Pacifism; Unusual Biochemistry*; Vow (Major; Never refuse a request for healing).<br /> <u>Psychic Vampirism:</u> Callous; Chummy<br /> or Gregarious (p. 6); Lifebane*; Uncontrollable Appetite (Life Force)*.<br /> <u>Psychokinesis:</u> Chronic Pain (p. 6); Pyromania; Trickster.<br /> <u>Telepathy:</u> Addiction (Telepathic Contact) (p. 5); Chummy or Gregarious (p. 6); Compulsive Snooping (p. 6); Phantom Voices; Supersensitive*.<br /> <u>Teleportation:</u> Overconfidence; Phobia<br /> (Enclosed Spaces); Sleepwalker.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, this small table was just a small sample of fitting disadvantages, but already we get plenty of information; for example, a few examples of &quot;psionic powers&quot;. <b>Anti-Psi</b>, the ability to nulify other psionic powers. This can be done with Countermagik (with Prime). <b>Astral Projection</b> - self explanatory (but the book have more examples of uses to that other than just getting your mind out of your body, such as &quot;astral possession&quot; and others). Mostly Mind 4 or 5. <b>Ergokinesis</b>. I'll be honest, I saw this a long time ago, but I dont remember what it is; Im not sure if it's electrical manipulation or something else, sorry. <b>ESP:</b> this is the power to &quot;see the unseen&quot;. Remote vision, looking into the future, precognition, that sort of things - divinations basically. <b>Probability Alteration:</b> this is a great one. Need I say anything else? Entropy all over. <b>Psychic Healing:</b> As the name says. Life 2 or 3 - but not only that. <b>Psychic Vampirism:</b> use Life and or Prime (or Spirit, or even matter perhaps) to &quot;suck the life force&quot; of others. Life + Prime can serve to &quot;fuel&quot; your own &quot;Quintessense&quot; (Psi Energy?) out of the life force of your victims. <b>Psychokinesis</b> - if Im not mistaken, this one cover Telekinesis, Pyrokinesis, Cryokinesis and a few others. It's basically the full range of Forces effects. <b>Telepathy</b> - that's perhaps the most famous psi abilities. Read and send thoughts, sometimes also control minds, etc etc. Mind Sphere all over. And <b>Teleport</b> is correspondence, althought the book has many clever uses of it besides just instant travel from point A to point B<br /> <br /> Edit: those Disadvantages above are also some interesting ideas for Permadox Flaws or Genetic Flaws, particularly for &quot;Psionic Constructs&quot; of the Union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 08-04-2022, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T10:10:14-07:00","id":1489128,"title":"","content":"Some additional powers deacribed on Gurps Psionic Powers (pag 72-75)<br /> Biokinesis<br /> Dream Control<br /> Psychometabolism<br /> <br /> Anyway, those 3 books contain a huge plethora of sample powers and abilities, how to use them and also applications of specific &quot;Psy-Tech&quot;.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, Ergokinesis by the way is indeed manipulation of electricity. And of particular interest in this is probably &quot;Cyber-Psy&quot;, the Psionic ability to control electronic devices (yes, computers), as a subset of Ergokinesis. Now, how to make use of those in Mage, Forces obviously, but particularly for Cyber-Psy, Entropy may also come in play (for hacking a computer with your brain instead of with code for example, Entropy 2, or Entropy 1 for &quot;guessing&quot; the password).<br /> <br /> So, all you need to know is figuring how to translate all of those into Spheres. I gave you a few examples but honestly, it's a lot for me to do that way. Another example - Psychic Vampirism: Steal Emotions - Mind 2, provokes a feeling of numbness and apathy in the victims, while the Mage gets to &quot;taste&quot; the victim's emotions. And so on, so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T07:14:57-07:00","id":1489480,"title":"","content":"So, I have one last thing to add.<br /> <br /> I have one &quot;Grand Theory of Psionics&quot; Paradigm.<br /> <br /> I designed this as a form for the Techies to explain the unexplainable &quot;Reality Deviants Phenomena&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, you guys are probably familiar with the idea of <b>Determinism</b>, which is a philosophical concept that became popular in the 19th century, at the high of classic physics. And in the 20th century, it gave way to <b>Quantum Determinism</b> (I'll leave aside the many quantum mechanics considerations for now thou).<br /> <br /> This also goes hand to hand with the math ideas os the <b>Chaos Theory</b>. Ever heard the expression &quot;A butterfly wings in the Atlantic causing hurricanes in the Pacific&quot;, or something similar?<br /> <br /> So, let me try to explain it all: the entire universe is interconnected; quantum mechanics even proved that it is connected in a quantum level. <br /> <br /> And it isnt hard to understand why or how. For example, our moon is far away, but it's gravity have direct influence on us. Venus, Mars, Jupiter, all the other planets also influence us, despite being even further away. Obviously the distance makes that influence be far less direct than our Moon, but it isnt null. Stars thousands of light years away have effects on us; cosmic rays, gravitational waves, some of those come from the beggining of the universe itself.<br /> <br /> Even the smallest grain of sand have gravity and electromagnetic fields which both influences and is influenced by the entire universe.<br /> <br /> Now, of course a grain of sand wont determine the ocean waves by itself alone; most of the time, all those tiny forces nullify one another, in a sort of &quot;background statics&quot;.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the human body (or any object really) also participates in this dance. Living beings segregate pheromones, we are constantly breathing in and out, and our minds produce an electromagnetic field of our own. We are, actively, constantly changing (and being changed) by the entire universe around us. That's too small of a change to be noticed thou, thus most of the times such &quot;disturbances&quot; are just nullified by the several countless others around.<br /> <br /> Here comes Psionics and Chaos Theory. Chaos Theory says that, the more interactions in a system, the harder it is to predict it's outcome. How could a butterfly generate hurricanes? The probability is minuscule, but possible. Imagine for example going back in time, perhaps some 1 million years, and killing one of the hominids that will be the ancestors of humanity. What would change?<br /> <br /> It's impossible to tell. Because that single being could be the ancestor of countless generations of people, and the entire human history could end up irrevocably altered by such a small event. A single baby living or dying - despite the fact that thousands are born or die every single day - could create a vast difference over thousands of years.<br /> <br /> Likewise, pulling a single grain of sand from a mountain, may cause an avalanche.<br /> <br /> In this vein is how Psionics work. A single thought, considering that a thought is an electric pulse in the brain, may cause just the right, the proper change of the electromagnetic field of the person that will ionize the air molecules around the person in just the proper way to cause some fantastic change around him/her.<br /> <br /> Now, the Psiquics do this in a subconcious way; conciously, they simply train their minds to operate in certain ways that allows them to achieve predetermined results.<br /> <br /> This is how &quot;Psionic Powers&quot; operate, the ultimate form of &quot;coincidences&quot;. It also explains basically ALL phenomena, from Paradox, to Consensus and to the abilities of the Reality Deviants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}